  "notes": "FORMS:\nFormed from {焼|や}く (to bake/grill) + たて (just done). The suffix たて attaches to the conjunctive form of verbs to mean \"just [verb]ed\" or \"freshly [verb]ed.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {焼|や}きたてのパン (freshly baked bread)\n- {焼|や}きたてのクッキー (freshly baked cookies)\n- {焼|や}きたての{魚|さかな} (freshly grilled fish)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {揚|あ}げたて: freshly fried\n- {炊|た}きたて: freshly cooked (rice)\n- {出来|でき}たて: freshly made",
